# The event bus in production (os-nats in deploy/compose.prod.yml, asafarim-os#259). Values never go in git as plaintext.
#
# 1. `node deploy/nats/new-env.mjs` writes core/nats/.env.production (git-ignored) with both values below, generated at
#    random, and adds core-api's side of the same login to core/core-api/.env.production (see deploy/README.md). It
#    refuses to overwrite an existing file.
# 2. `pnpm env:encrypt:production` writes core/nats/.env.production.age: commit only that (in a pull request).
# 3. The next full deploy, with core-api's env as well, decrypts it into .env.nats and starts os-nats. A commit without
#    the .age file deploys exactly as before, without it.
#
# This container reads ONLY these two names. The auth callout's signing key (the seed) is not here: it stays in
# core-api's env, so the bus holds the public half only.

# The auth callout issuer's PUBLIC key (an account nkey: starts with A). NATS trusts answers signed by its seed.
NATS_AUTH_ISSUER=
# core-api's own login on the bus (user `core`): the only user that skips the callout.
NATS_CORE_PASSWORD=
